I went into a bookstore and read a spellbook. It was a teleport spell,
so I got teleported out of the store without paying for it. Then the
cops came after me. Killed a few (thrilled my subversive ol' heart no
end) then tried to bribe the sergeant by throwing some $ at him. He
still came after me.

So my question is: where does the dev team get off with this
uncorruptible cop business? What's this country coming to when you
can't even bribe a cop into letting you off? The next version should
have the Kops, when they've been idle too long, setting up a protection
racket with the orcs selling crack (unholy water) at street (corridor)
corners. And occasionally beating up a passing hobbit. Come to think of
it, you could then have a Tourist passing by with his camera, and if he
manages to film it, he gets the Amulet and gets crowned King Yendor.

(For the anagram-deficient, that's Rodney King spelt backwards, sort of.)

